\section{Entrainment-Mediated Tropical-Cyclone Intensification}\label{30005987}

\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


Entrainment is the incorporation of surrounding air into a rising cloud tower. The proposed asymptotic mechanism creates a radial mean flow and transports angular momentum toward the cyclone center. A three-dimensional resolved simulation can test these fluxes and the predicted change in cyclone strength.

\paragraph{Catalogue wording retained for traceability.}
Using three-dimensional high-resolution simulations, verify the asymptotically derived pathway in which cloud-tower entrainment produces a radial mean flow that transports angular momentum inward and intensifies a tropical cyclone.

\paragraph{Scope and source qualification.}The source requests physical-model validation, not a proof for an unspecified universal PDE. The asymptotic pathway and simulated observables must be compared in the source regime.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Test the proposed cloud-entrainment pathway to cyclone intensification using high-resolution three-dimensional simulations.

\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived parcel spin-up under conserved angular momentum and the mean-flux correlation term needed to test the proposed entrainment pathway.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30005987. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{The kinematic spin-up implication.} In an axisymmetric inviscid test model on a constant Coriolis parameter \(f\), let \(r\) be radius, \(u=dr/dt\) radial velocity, and \(v\) tangential velocity. Specific absolute angular momentum is \(L=rv+fr^2/2\). If a parcel conserves \(L\), differentiation gives
\[
 \frac{dv}{dt}=-\left(\frac vr+f\right)u.
\]
For \(r>0\), \(u<0\) and \(v/r+f>0\), inward motion increases tangential speed. Equivalently \(v(r)=L/r-fr/2\) along the parcel, so the sign test is exact within these assumptions.
\paragraph{Why mean inflow alone is insufficient.} In a local incompressible axisymmetric angular-momentum balance,
\[
 \partial_t L+\frac1r\partial_r(ruL)+\partial_z(wL)=0,
\]
where \(w\) is vertical velocity. Averaging a fluctuating flow yields \(\overline{uL}=\bar u\,\bar L+\overline{u'L'}\), with primes denoting deviations from the averaging operation. Therefore a measured negative \(\bar u\) does not by itself identify the mean angular-momentum flux: the correlation term and vertical flux remain. In a compressible simulation the corresponding mass-weighted conservation law must be used instead.
\paragraph{Actual validation gap.} This derivation checks one link in the proposed entrainment pathway and specifies fluxes whose omission could produce a misleading test. It does not show that entrainment creates the inflow or that the total torque/flux budget intensifies a simulated cyclone. No three-dimensional high-resolution simulation was run. The first missing work is resolving those source-regime entrainment and momentum budgets, their errors and convergence, in the requested simulations; algebraic parcel spin-up is not physical validation.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked differentiation of absolute momentum, sign conditions, radial geometry, mean-product decomposition and the distinction between incompressible and mass-weighted budgets. Model self-audit only; no independent human mathematical verification. Applied contribution prompt A before drafting and B afterwards. Checked differentiation of absolute momentum, sign conditions, radial geometry, mean-product decomposition and the distinction between incompressible and mass-weighted budgets. First remaining gap: Run and resolve the source-regime three-dimensional entrainment and angular-momentum budgets with numerical error and resolution checks. The inherited source status is preserved; original-target completion remains zero.

Coordinator checked the conserved parcel angular-momentum derivative and unresolved averaged correlation flux. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file tools used to read definitions and serialize manuscripts. Calculations are symbolic reasoning; no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Run and resolve the source-regime three-dimensional entrainment and angular-momentum budgets with numerical error and resolution checks.

